  "solution": {
    "approach": "The problem only requires comparing two integers and printing the larger one. For each test case we read the two numbers, evaluate the boolean expression (a>b) and use a switch statement on its integer value (1 for true, 0 for false). The switch selects the appropriate branch and appends the larger value to the output. This runs in O(1) per test case, total O(T) time, and uses O(1) extra space.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(T) total, O(1) per test case",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1) besides the output buffer",
    "code": {
      "C": "",
      "C++": "",
      "Java": "import java.io.*;import java.util.*;public class Main{public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException{BufferedReader br=new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));StringBuilder sb=new StringBuilder();int T=Integer.parseInt(br.readLine().trim());for(int i=0;i<T;i++){StringTokenizer st=new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());int a=Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());int b=Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());switch(a>b?1:0){case 1:sb.append(a);break;default:sb.append(b);}if(i<T-1)sb.append('\\n');}System.out.print(sb.toString());}}",
      "Python3": "",
      "JavaScript": ""
    },
